From 34f16d1ddc96f8966866647d229d87e1fcab45a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rock-5b: enable vendor U-Boot serial console

The ROCK 5B current and vendor targets use Radxa U-Boot's
rock-5b-rk3588_defconfig, which selects all three relevant options:

    CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=0
    CONFIG_DISABLE_CONSOLE=y
    CONFIG_SYS_CONSOLE_INFO_QUIET=y

DISABLE_CONSOLE disables console input and output completely.  The INFO_QUIET
option is narrower: it suppresses the stdin/stdout/stderr device summary after
relocation.  BOOTDELAY=0 is independent of both; it checks for input but
provides no intentional countdown delay.

In Radxa's Rockchip code, both SPL and U-Boot proper turn DISABLE_CONSOLE into
GD_FLG_DISABLE_CONSOLE.  The console and NS16550 paths then reject input and
drop output while that flag is set, so a longer delay alone cannot make the
UART prompt usable.

The vendor settings are not a general quiet-mode convention.  Radxa's
next-dev-v2024.10 has 1,317 defconfigs: 101 select delay zero, 251 select
SYS_CONSOLE_INFO_QUIET, but only one selects DISABLE_CONSOLE -- ROCK 5B.
Radxa commit 0d3169e641d added that line with the subject
"rock-5b-rk3588_defconfig: disable console" and no further rationale.  It is
still the only disabled-console defconfig among the 1,326 configs in
next-dev-v2026.01.

BOOTDELAY is a separate Armbian policy question.  Across config/ at 61ba9d2a0
there are 60 BOOTDELAY assignments: 57 select one second, two select two
seconds, and the only zero is the shared rockchip64 common value.  That value
now feeds five family configs containing 163 board descriptors.  Changing it
belongs in a separately tested fleet-wide change, not this console fix.

Upstream v2026.01 rock5b-rk3588_defconfig selects neither console-suppression
option.  Armbian also has direct precedent for reversing Radxa's choice:
9ff15f7896 ("hinlink-h88k: enable uboot serial log") removes the same two
options from another Radxa-tree board.

Remove both console-suppression options in a board-scoped Radxa U-Boot patch.
Leave BOOTDELAY unchanged: it is separately imposed by Armbian's shared
rockchip64 policy, while the edge target retains its existing one-second
override and upstream U-Boot.

The outer patch passes git apply --check against armbian/build main at
61ba9d2a0.  The embedded patch passes against Radxa next-dev-v2024.10, whose
defconfig preimage is 6832279aad6.  Not built or boot-tested.

Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 .../board_rock-5b/enable-serial-console.patch | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 patch/u-boot/legacy/u-boot-radxa-rk35xx/board_rock-5b/enable-serial-console.patch

diff --git a/patch/u-boot/legacy/u-boot-radxa-rk35xx/board_rock-5b/enable-serial-console.patch b/patch/u-boot/legacy/u-boot-radxa-rk35xx/board_rock-5b/enable-serial-console.patch
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..1e2ed6889
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patch/u-boot/legacy/u-boot-radxa-rk35xx/board_rock-5b/enable-serial-console.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+diff --git a/configs/rock-5b-rk3588_defconfig b/configs/rock-5b-rk3588_defconfig
+index 6832279aad6..f631f614b74 100644
+--- a/configs/rock-5b-rk3588_defconfig
++++ b/configs/rock-5b-rk3588_defconfig
+@@ -33,8 +33,6 @@ CONFIG_SPL_FIT_IMAGE_POST_PROCESS=y
+ CONFIG_SPL_FIT_HW_CRYPTO=y
+ # CONFIG_SPL_SYS_DCACHE_OFF is not set
+ CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=0
+-CONFIG_DISABLE_CONSOLE=y
+-CONFIG_SYS_CONSOLE_INFO_QUIET=y
+ # CONFIG_DISPLAY_CPUINFO is not set
+ CONFIG_ANDROID_BOOTLOADER=y
+ CONFIG_ANDROID_AVB=y
-- 
